# One historical finding, not a blanket allowlist.
#
# GoldenWireTests used the fixture "pk_live_abc.s3cr3t". It is not a credential —
# it never authenticated anything, and the test only needs a value of the form
# prefix.secret. But "pk_live_" is the prefix a live Stripe-style key carries, so
# gitleaks' generic-api-key rule matched it, correctly on its face.
#
# The fixtures are now "examplePrefix.exampleSecret", so nothing committed from
# here on matches. The scan reads full history, so the original commit keeps
# reporting until that history is rewritten; this pins the single fingerprint
# rather than muting the rule, a path, or a file.
#
# Remove this line if the branch is ever squashed or rewritten — it stops being
# needed the moment that commit is gone.
